{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310820,"nonce":"HhjqpmP9q9zi5fdIazj0f6lR0ag=","title":"L8 RESOLVED — Arc/Mutex are now REAL (thread-safe) on wasm via in-guest shared-memory atomics in runtime-wasm; replaces the host-side fakes","message":"**L8 from [[perf_rayzor_namespace_near_native]] CLOSED (uncommitted, branch wasm-default-inguest-matmul, on top of atomics commit c1d1d890).** rayzor.concurrent.Arc and Mutex were FAKE on wasm — Arc was an identity pass-through with `strong_count` hard-wired to 1 (no refcount), Mutex was a non-atomic `bool` in the MAIN instance's host `WasmState.mutex_handles` BTreeMap. **Now both are real**, implemented in-guest in `runtime-wasm/src/concurrent.rs` (NEW) + `lib.rs` (`pub mod concurrent;` + `#![cfg_attr(target_arch=\"wasm32\", feature(stdarch_wasm_atomic_wait))]`).\n\n**THE decisive architecture fact (why in-guest, not host-fake-with-atomics):** worker threads build a bare `Linker\u003c()\u003e` with `define_unknown_imports_as_traps` (wasm_runner.rs worker_main) — they NEVER get the host Arc/Mutex shims, so a host-side impl only exists on the MAIN instance and every worker that touched Arc/Mutex would TRAP. The wasm_linker MERGES runtime-wasm into the user module, so symbols defined there become INTERNAL guest functions present in the main AND every worker instance, all over the one SharedMemory. This is the same mechanism the Tensor `refcount: AtomicUsize` (tensor.rs) already uses. So it's a runtime-wasm-ONLY change — no compiler/stdlib/codegen edit (the externs in stdlib/sync.rs already emit identical CallDirects for both backends; native backs them with std::sync::Arc + parking_lot, wasm now backs the SAME names in-guest).\n\n**Design:** Arc = 8-byte cell `[strong:AtomicU32 @+0, value:i32 @+4]`; clone = `fetch_add(1,Relaxed)` returning the SAME handle, drop = `fetch_sub(1,Release)`+Acquire-fence-on-last, try_unwrap = `CAS(1,0)`. Mutex = `[state:AtomicU32 @+0, value @+4]`, canonical Mara-Bos **3-state futex** (0/1/2): fast-path CAS, bounded spin, then `memory.atomic.wait32` park; unlock = `swap(0,Release)` + `memory.atomic.notify(1)` only if prior==2. Guard == mutex handle. Also added real sys.thread.Mutex (sys_mutex_alloc/acquire/try_acquire/release reusing the cell). New `rayzor_arc_drop` symbol exists+testable but compiler emits NO drop yet (count climbs monotonically — IDENTICAL to native's missing-drop gap, not a new leak).\n\n**THE #1 ABI GATE (cost-free to get wrong, silent):** ir_type_to_wasm lowers PtrU8/U64/Bool ALL to i32 and Void to no-result; a runtime-wasm fn whose wasm sig differs is SILENTLY stubbed to unreachable by wasm_linker pass-A. So `rayzor_arc_strong_count`/`as_ptr` return **i32** (NOT the native u64) and `rayzor_mutex_unlock` returns **`()`** (NOT i32). Also: cast handles `i32 as u32 as usize` (NOT `as usize`) or the 2^31 signed-pointer boundary sign-extends and the deref goes wild (\u003e2GB heap).\n\n**Verified (3-gate):** (1) algorithm proven race-free on host via a standalone mirror — 8 threads × 50k Arc clone/drop → strong_count exactly 1; 8 × 100k Mutex-guarded increments → exactly 800000 (no lost updates). The crate itself does NOT build for host (pre-existing `rayzor_host_flash_attn_q8_par` cfg gap) so in-crate `cargo test` is unrunnable — used the standalone proof. (2) objdump: linked module emits i32.atomic.rmw.add/sub/cmpxchg/xchg + memory.atomic.wait32/notify over `(memory ... shared)`, NO residual `(import \"rayzor\" \"rayzor_arc/mutex\")` (all resolved internal). (3) e2e `rayzor run --wasm` of an Arc/Mutex Haxe program == native byte-for-byte (strongCount 1→2→3 = real, fake was constant 1). Multi-thread HAXE driver still blocked by the orthogonal E0100 closure-capture bug, so Haxe-level coverage is single-thread; the cross-thread guarantee rests on the host algorithm proof + the shared-memory topology (worker pool already proves wasm shared atomics work).\n\n**Left as-is / follow-ups:** host Arc/Mutex fakes in wasm_runner.rs:3613-3824 + MutexState:630 are now DEAD (linker resolves to internal; linked module has zero rayzor_arc imports) but kept as a harmless fallback — optional cleanup. Build: must run `runtime-wasm/build.sh` (cargo +nightly) to regen the gitignored artifact at runtime-wasm/target/wasm32-wasip1-threads/release/rayzor_runtime_wasm.wasm (find_wasm_runtime searches that path first). NOT yet committed.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_wasm_real_arc_mutex` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}